        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS proudly present this wonderful three-bedroom detached cottage perfectly located in the heart of Saggart Village, Co Dublin. The village of Saggart has plenty to recommend for home buyers, especially those looking to move out of the city. It retains a rural feel despite being close to the city, with some beautiful scenery nearby and an abundance of local amenities including schools, shops and eateries. Transport wise, the location is next to none as the area is well serviced by excellent transport links from numerous bus routes to the Red Line Luas just a 5-minute walk away. \r\n\r\nBright, airy and most spacious living accommodation of c. 86 sqm compromises of entrance hallway, three double bedrooms, open plan living/kitchen area with beautiful solid fuel log burner and main family bathroom. You benefit from a high degree of privacy here. To the rear of the property you have a lovely low maintenance garden that would have the potential to be extended on in the future. The front of the property offers off street parking for two cars. \r\n\r\nThe Refuge is presented in great condition throughout having been lovingly maintained by its current owner and has a long list of additional features such as double-glazed windows, gas fired central heating and recently renovated bathroom to name but a few. It is situated in one of Saggarts most sought after areas and we will expect lots of interest from a wide range of buyers. Viewing is highly advised to fully appreciate the benefits that this fantastic home has to offer. \r\n\r\nAdditional Features; \r\n- E2 BER \r\n- C 86 sqm \r\n- 3 bed 1 bath \r\n- Detached cottage \r\n- Scope for extension in the future \r\n- Large open plan kitchen/living area\r\n- Fully fitted kitchen \r\n- Solid fuel log burner \r\n- Three generous bedrooms \r\n- Main family bathroom \r\n- Recently renovated \r\n- Double glazed windows \r\n- Top quality blinds \r\n- Gas fired central heating \r\n- Low maintenance rear garden \r\n- Sunny orientation \r\n- Designated parking off street \r\n- Immaculately presented throughout \r\n- Close to all local amenities \r\n- 5-minute walk to Saggart luas stop \r\n- Viewing is highly advised \r\n\r\nDirections - Coming off the N7 at the Rathcoole/Saggart junction, take the first exit onto Mill road towards Saggart. Take the first exit at the next roundabout you reach and proceed towards village. At the cross roads, take a left turn where The Refuge will be clearly sign posted on the right."
      },
